{"timestamp":1789670638,"method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"01a0b0ae-1a4e-7f23-a69a-96157c01338c","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_message_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"The `docs` folder in this repository holds eleven durable reference files rather than dated notes or plans. It includes `architecture.mmd`, a hand-authored Mermaid diagram of the launcher’s process split, FastAPI routers, and shared `src/` library; `board.md` for the fleet kanban; `cache-hygiene-asset-hashing.md` for static-asset hashing; `ci-github-actions.md` for the GitHub Actions e2e job; `detached-stop-decision.md` for how detached session-host processes are stopped; `iphone-debugging.md` for phone debugging; `jobs-tab.md` for the Jobs tab; `launcher-owned-pty.md` for the Coding PTY layer; `pi-coding-agent.md` for the Pi harness; `restart-and-liveness.md` for tray restart and `/api/version` liveness; and `voice-loop-spike.md` for a voice-loop experiment. Together they describe architecture, tab behavior, process ownership, CI, and operator recipes that a later reader would reopen, not a changelog of closed issues.\n\nA dedicated docs folder matters because GitHub issues and pull requests already own decisions, while the tree still needs a stable place for design records, architecture overviews, integration guides, and shared playbooks. Putting those topics under `docs/` with topic filenames instead of dates keeps usage, config, and restart rules findable without burying them in chat or in `README.md` alone. This repo’s own instructions say `docs/` is for durable reference a future agent or human will re-open, and they pair that with an anti-staleness contract: `architecture.mmd` is updated in the same change as a structural shift, and `restart-and-liveness.md` is the recipe after the verification gate. Without that folder, operators would hunt through CLAUDE.md, README, and issue threads for the same facts, and those facts would drift.\n\nThe folder also separates product documentation from code and from ephemeral planning. Source under `app/` and `src/` answers how the webapp and session-host work; `docs/` answers why a process is detached, how iPhone debugging is done, how the Jobs tab is meant to be used, and how CI is expected to behave. That split is especially useful in a multi-agent fleet where each session starts cold: a well-named markdown file plus a README pointer is cheaper than re-deriving procedure from a prior agent’s diff. The presence of both operational runbooks (`restart-and-liveness.md`, `iphone-debugging.md`) and conceptual records (`detached-stop-decision.md`, `launcher-owned-pty.md`) shows the folder is meant to survive the next issue, not to track work in flight. Keeping it read-only in this turn matches that role: list what is there, explain it, and leave the files untouched."}},"_meta":{"totalTokens":31102,"eventId":"01a0b0ae-1a4e-7f23-a69a-96157c01338c-710","agentTimestampMs":1789670637505,"promptId":"59b7c5a7-6cea-4e28-a5d3-f108627c727d","streamStartMs":1789670624710,"turnStartMs":1789670620392,"updateType":"AgentMessageChunk","chunkId":627}}}
